winewayland: never attach a buffer before the surface has an xdg role

xdg-shell requires that a surface have no buffer attached when a role is assigned, and
that nothing be committed before the first xdg_surface.configure. wayland_window_surface_flush
did not check, so a WS_EX_LAYERED window -- whose content arrives via UpdateLayeredWindow
BEFORE the window is shown -- attached a buffer while the surface was still roleless.

Reproduced by the build tester 3/3 on 11.10-69 and -70 (Premiere's splash, hwnd 0x70246):

  CreateWindowSurface  layered 1
  clear_role           surface has NO role
  attach_shm           <<< BUFFER ATTACHED
  make_toplevel        <<< ROLE, 8 ms LATER

The guard mirrors the existing wayland_window_can_commit() bail in the same function: return
FALSE and let win32u retry. Verified on the dev box -- the attach now lands after make_toplevel,
on the first configure, and costs exactly 2 deferrals for the splash (print capped at 20, so
the count is exact, not sampled). Content still arrives 8 ms later; nothing is lost.

Kill switch: NEUTRON_ROLE_GATE=0 restores the old unguarded flush.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
@@ -577,6 +577,7 @@
 struct wayland_shm_buffer *get_window_surface_contents(HWND hwnd);
 void ensure_window_surface_contents(HWND hwnd);
 BOOL wayland_window_can_commit(HWND hwnd);
+BOOL wayland_window_surface_has_role(HWND hwnd);
 
 /**********************************************************************
  *          Wayland Keyboard
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -1837,6 +1837,32 @@
 /* NEUTRON M2: TRUE if a commit for this window would currently succeed. Lets the SHM flush
  * skip the (tens-of-MB at 4K) buffer copies it would otherwise do and then discard, during the
  * maximize/un-maximize transition when the xdg config isn't compatible yet. Read-only. */
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           wayland_window_surface_has_role
+ *
+ * NEUTRON: has this window's wayland surface been given an xdg role yet?
+ *
+ * A wl_surface with no role must not have a buffer attached -- xdg-shell requires the surface to be
+ * unmapped and buffer-less when the role is assigned, and forbids committing content before the
+ * first xdg_surface.configure. See role_guard.py for the measured violation this exists to stop.
+ *
+ * Returns TRUE when there is no surface at all, so windows the driver is not managing are
+ * unaffected and behave exactly as before.
+ */
+BOOL wayland_window_surface_has_role(HWND hwnd)
+{
+    struct wayland_surface *surface;
+    struct wayland_win_data *data;
+    BOOL has = TRUE;
+
+    if (!(data = wayland_win_data_get(hwnd))) return TRUE;
+    if ((surface = data->wayland_surface))
+        has = surface->role != WAYLAND_SURFACE_ROLE_NONE;
+    wayland_win_data_release(data);
+
+    return has;
+}
+
 BOOL wayland_window_can_commit(HWND hwnd)
 {
     struct wayland_surface *surface;
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window_surface.c
@@ -448,6 +448,39 @@
     if (!wayland_window_can_commit(window_surface->hwnd))
         return FALSE;
 
+    /* NEUTRON: never attach a buffer to a surface that has no xdg role yet.
+     *
+     * MEASURED on a tester's machine 2026-09-01, 3/3 runs: for Premiere's LAYERED splash the chain
+     * CreateWindowSurface(layered=1) -> wayland_window_surface_flush -> wayland_surface_reconfigure
+     * -> wayland_surface_attach_shm ran ~8 ms BEFORE wayland_surface_make_toplevel. xdg-shell
+     * forbids that: the surface must be buffer-less when the role is assigned and must not commit
+     * before the first xdg_surface.configure.
+     *
+     * Layered windows are the ones that hit it because their content arrives via
+     * UpdateLayeredWindow BEFORE the window is shown, rather than via a paint afterwards.
+     *
+     * Same bail as can_commit above: win32u keeps the bounds dirty and flushes again once the role
+     * exists, so nothing is lost.
+     *
+     * Kill switch NEUTRON_ROLE_GATE=0 restores the old behaviour for A/B. */
+    {
+        static int gate = -1;
+        if (gate < 0)
+        {
+            const char *e = getenv("NEUTRON_ROLE_GATE");
+            gate = (e && e[0] == '0') ? 0 : 1;
+        }
+        if (gate && !wayland_window_surface_has_role(window_surface->hwnd))
+        {
+            static LONG deferred;
+            if (InterlockedIncrement(&deferred) <= 20)
+                ERR("neutron-rolegate: hwnd=%p DEFERRING flush -- surface has no xdg role yet "
+                    "(attaching now would violate xdg-shell); win32u will retry\n",
+                    window_surface->hwnd);
+            return FALSE;
+        }
+    }
+
     surface_damage_region = NtGdiCreateRectRgn(rect->left + dirty->left, rect->top + dirty->top,
                                                rect->left + dirty->right, rect->top + dirty->bottom);
     if (!surface_damage_region)
